## Message Flow Architecture

### Control Flow (Android → ESP32)

```
1. User Action
   ├── MainActivity.onClick()
   │
2. Command Generation
   ├── toggleDevice(device)
   ├── Generate: "kitchen_light_on"
   │
3. MQTT Publish
   ├── MqttService.publishMessage()
   ├── Topic: "smarthome/control"
   │
4. MQTT Broker
   ├── broker.hivemq.com:1883
   ├── Route to subscribed clients
   │
5. ESP32 Receives
   ├── mqttCallback()
   ├── handleLightControl()
   │
6. GPIO Control
   ├── setLight(room, state)
   ├── digitalWrite(RELAY1, LOW)  // Active LOW
   │
7. Physical Action
   └── Relay activates → Light turns ON
```

### Status Flow (ESP32 → Android)

```
1. ESP32 State Change
   ├── Physical relay state updated
   │
2. Status Generation
   ├── publishStatus()
   ├── JSON: {"kitchen_light":"on", ...}
   │
3. MQTT Publish
   ├── Topic: "smarthome/status"
   ├── Retained: true
   │
4. MQTT Broker
   ├── Store retained message
   ├── Forward to subscribers
   │
5. Android Receives
   ├── MqttService.onMessageReceived()
   ├── MainActivity.parseStatusMessage()
   │
6. UI Update
   ├── Update Device states
   ├── deviceAdapter.notifyDataSetChanged()
   │
7. Visual Feedback
   └── Switch toggles, indicator changes color
```

